        {
          "id": "S001",
          "text": "Work with the smooth trajectory N007. Assume L1: the step comparison conditions of the output. Put w=v(t_n), f=v^n, delta_n=||f-w||_2 and q_n=tau^gamma+delta_n<=2. H001 fixes the exponent. The definition of Res concatenates increments rho_n with rho_n(t_n)=0; thus Res is continuous piecewise smooth with Res(0)=0. N007 gives V'=B_t(z_n,z_n)/2-W_n/tau. Expanding V=z_n+Y_n proves V'=B_t(V,V)/2+Res', with Res'=-B_t(Y_n,z_n)-B_t(Y_n,Y_n)/2-W_n/tau.",
