          "text": "Apply the N006 normal form to the first integral in rho_n. Since Y_n(t_n)=0, its endpoint bound is C||Dinv Y_n||_2||z_n||_2<=C_M tau q_n by N008. The derivative integral with Y_n' is <=C tau sup||Dinv Y_n'||_2 sup||z_n||_2<=C_M tau q_n. Since z_n'=B_t(f,f)/2, the other derivative term is a constant times C_[t_n,t](f,f,Y_n); N005 with negative norm on Y_n bounds it by C_M tau q_n using both ||Y_n||_X<=C_M q_n and ||Y_n||_H^(-pstar)<=C_M tau q_n. Apply N006 again to the integral with two Y_n slots. Its endpoint and derivative terms are each O(tau q_n^2), by N008, and q_n<=2 makes this O(tau q_n). The affine W_n term is <=||W_n||_2<=C_M tau q_n. This proves sup||rho_n||_2<=C_M tau q_n at every partial endpoint. Finally F001 and the B bound N006 give ||Res'||_H^(-pstar)<=C_M(q_n+q_n^2)+||W_n||_2/tau<=C_M q_n. Discharge L1 to obtain the conditional bounds, together with the unconditional residual identities, in the output.",
